{"task": "IG-2B07", "path": "docs/IG-DATA-MODEL.md", "start_line": 1, "lines": ["# IG data contract proposal", "", "This document consolidates the earlier `ig-draft-0.2` design. It is not a machine schema", "or accepted game semantics. IG-1A establishes the source contract; IG-3A establishes", "the executable language after source reconciliation. See [architecture](IG-WGU-ARCHITECTURE.md).", "", "## Identity and record envelope", "", "Each record has stable `id`, `record_type`, `schema_version`, `revision_id`, `run_id`,", "`supersedes_refs`, and canonical content hash. Stable identity is separate from revision,", "file path, array position and content hash. External WGU IDs are namespaced by KB.", "`origin_bindings` link many-to-many IG IDs to input snapshot/file/field locators.", "Anonymous terms and relations use a persisted identity registry; ambiguous rematches", "become conflicts. Split/merge lineage does not transfer acceptance automatically.", "", "References used as active rules resolve only in the selected snapshot. Historical", "review and supersession references resolve in an immutable revision store. A snapshot", "selects at most one revision per ID, but may retain conflicting assertions with different", "IDs. The presence of an old revision does not activate it. Namespaced IDs must be safely", "encoded as Windows file names rather than used literally with colons.", "", "## Collections and invariants", "", "| Collection | Minimum content and constraints |", "|---|---|", "| sources / artifacts | Role, publisher/system/edition/language, part, media type, bytes, SHA-256, availability and compatibility |", "| regions / evidence | Source revision, PDF page (1-based), printed label, reading order, coordinate/offset convention, precise region links |", "| nodes | Sections, clauses, concepts, procedures/steps, tables/axes/cells, diagrams, components and mechanical definitions |", "| assertions | Subject, stable aspect, knowledge state, literal/normalized/interpreted representation, value, scope, evidence and gaps |", "| semantic_groups | Stable aspect IDs and explicit condition/effect/exception/timing composition |", "| relations | Typed directed link, applicability, target status, candidates, evidence, requirement grouping |", "| gaps | Missing source, unreadable, unprocessed, ambiguity, conflict or unsupported interpretation; affected targets and blocked operations |", "| profiles | System, edition, rules mode, options, scenario, maps/counters, pinned materials and compatibility decisions |", "| reviews | Exact targets and basis revisions, kind, actor role, decision/observation, scope and supersession |", "| coverage | Inventory revision, region, representation level, status and exclusion reason |", "| snapshots | Selected revisions and hashes, profile, conflicts, manifest and independent readiness reports |", "| runs / evaluation | Raw proposals, context manifest, actual configuration evidence, measurements and independently justified expectations |", "", "`sources.role`: rulebook, errata, faq, scenario, map, counter_sheet, player_aid, other.", "Edition labels do not establish compatibility. Exact transcription, normalization,", "uncertain symbols and interpretation remain distinguishable. Evidence roles are direct,", "context and counterevidence. Attaching a whole page does not prove every assertion.", "", "Nodes include action, event_type, state_variable, resource, timing_window, choice,", "selector, spatial_policy, randomizer, calculation and outcome. Their source representation", "may precede formal execution. A generic payload field alone is not demonstrated support.", "Editorial parentage is not an execution dependency. Clause boundaries preserve complete", "conditions and effects; aspects can be separately reviewed inside a container revision.", "", "## Knowledge and representation", "", "Knowledge states: `known` (evidenced proposal, review separate), `established_absent`", "(source proves absence in an explicit scope), `unknown` (null plus gap/reason), and", "`not_applicable` (null plus reason). Missing fields and empty lists never prove absence.", "Representations: literal, normalized, interpreted. A normative assertion has an explicit", "execution impact: formal, informational with reviewed rationale, or blocking.", "", "Facets include transcription, condition, effect, parameter, exception, timing, scope,", "definition, permission, obligation, prohibition, trigger, cost, choice, calculation,", "transition, duration, aggregation, visibility and victory. A shared subject ID does", "not bind several conditions to the right effects; semantic groups do that explicitly.", "Units, comparison operators, rounding stage, temporal bounds and causal filters are typed.", "Opaque is preserved text with an execution limitation, never a runtime LLM callback.", "", "## Relations", "", "Navigation (`mention`) is distinct from dependency (`procedure_use`, `table_use`,", "`definition`, `condition`). Exception/modification points from modifying rule to base.", "`applies_to` points from clause to scope object; `illustrates` from example to rule;", "`precedes` from earlier to later step with its condition. `continuation` alone is not", "an executable stack frame. Mechanical relations are specified in the mechanics contract.", "", "`target_status`: resolved, unresolved, ambiguous, unsupported. Non-resolved references", "retain raw locator, edition, candidate IDs and a gap. Targets can select exact aspects.", "`requirement`: required, conditional, informational; groups explicitly specify all/any.", "Unknown applicability cannot be treated as false. Rule graphs may contain cycles;", "the task dependency graph may not. Procedure cycles need termination/continuation rules.", "", "## Reviews and readiness", ""], "truncated": true}

